26	// pointer. One sweep examines each entry at most once per window: an entry
27	// that does not fit is left in place and can never become admissible later
28	// in the same window (pool and gate usage only grow until the next flip),
29	// while the sweep moves on so younger, fitting requests pass it. New
30	// arrivals are appended, expiries unlink in O(1), which keeps the
31	// acquire/release hot path constant-amortized. At every flip the scan
32	// pointer returns to the head, so the oldest waiting entry gets the very
33	// first pick of a fresh window - the guarantee that no request, however
34	// large, is ever starved.
35	function drainFamily(family) {
36	  let entry = family.scan;
